\mathbb{E}[N_{\text{replaced}}] = N_{\text{tiles}} \times (1 - P_{\text{survive}}(1)) \approx 4\,000 \times 10^{-4} = 0.4 \ \text{tiles per flight}.
\]

The stated 15 % tile replacement figure represents a conservative operational scenario where tiles are replaced preventively based on ultrasonic guided wave inspection with crack detection sensitivity of 2 mm, providing ample warning margin before structural failure.

