### 4.2.3 Water Extraction Thermodynamics

The thermal energy required to extract water from hydrated regolith is dominated by the sensible heat to raise the bulk material from the mean surface temperature (−60 °C, 213 K) to the sublimation point and the latent heat of phase change. For 3 wt % ice content, producing 1 kg of water requires processing approximately 33.3 kg of regolith:

\[
Q_{\text{extraction}} = m_{\text{regolith}}\, c_p\, \Delta T + m_{\text{water}} (L_{\text{fus}} + L_{\text{vap}}).
