## 12.5 Digital Twin as Integration Backbone

The digital twin serves as the integration backbone that transforms STARSHIP‑X from a collection of independent subsystems into a coherent cyber‑physical organism. The spacecraft digital twin platform described in recent literature supports multiple application scenarios — on‑orbit mission simulation and emulation, real‑time interactive monitoring, and fast operating condition prediction — enabling system‑level digital operation for subsystems including energy, power, control, and communication. STARSHIP‑X extends this paradigm by incorporating the crew as an integral component of the digital twin ecosystem.

The recently proposed Interaction Digital Twin (IDT) framework twins the interactions between humans and systems rather than focusing only on individual entities. Built on a distributed digital twin architecture with bidirectional information flow, the framework integrates three complementary types of twins: Digital Twins for habitat systems, Human Digital Twins for individual crew members, and Interaction Digital Twins that capture emergent phenomena such as team cohesion, trust calibration, coordination, and adaptive autonomy. Twinning the interactions moves aspects of command and control onboard, giving crew mission‑control‑like capabilities even during periods of communication delay. The STARSHIP‑X digital twin architecture, with its Kalman‑filtered thermal‑structural ROM, LSTM‑autoencoder anomaly detector, GP regression drift monitor, and Markov health‑state model, implements precisely this vision.

The cyber‑physical testbed developed for smart and resilient space habitats demonstrates that digital twin construction and updating, fault detection and diagnosis, decision‑making, and state estimation can be integrated into a unified experimental platform. The HabSim testbed at Purdue University has specifically validated that modular simulation architectures support systematic investigations of emergent behaviours and complex failure modes that are intrinsic to space habitat systems. These testbed results provide independent experimental validation of the digital‑twin‑centric integration philosophy that underpins the STARSHIP‑X architecture.

