# APPENDIX O — FAILURE MODE AND EFFECTS ANALYSIS (FMEA)

A comprehensive Failure Mode and Effects Analysis has been conducted for all catastrophic and critical hazards identified in the STARSHIP‑X architecture. The FMEA follows the framework of NASA‑STD‑8719.24 (NASA System Safety Handbook) and employs standard severity and likelihood categories.

**Hazard H‑1: Loss of Crew (LOC) during Mars EDL.**  
*Causes:* HIAD inflation failure; SRP engine failure; terrain‑relative navigation fault; plume‑induced instability.  
*Controls:* Redundant inflation gas generators; engine‑out vCBF‑guided abort; Mars 2020‑heritage LVS with 5 m accuracy; validated CFD model with 25 % margin.  
*Severity:* Catastrophic (1). *Likelihood:* Remote (D). *Risk Index:* 1D (acceptable with verification).

**Hazard H‑2: Radiation‑induced medical incapacitation of crew.**  
*Causes:* Solar particle event (SPE) exceeding shielding capacity; GCR cumulative dose exceeding career limit.  
*Controls:* Storm shelter with 20 g/cm² shielding; active dosimetry; reactor shadow shield; Van‑Allen belt transit trajectory optimisation.  
*Severity:* Catastrophic (1). *Likelihood:* Remote (D). *Risk Index:* 1D.

**Hazard H‑3: ISRU return‑fuel production failure.**  
*Causes:* Sabatier catalyst poisoning; water‑ice deposit exhaustion; mining rover fleet immobilisation.  
*Controls:* Redundant catalyst beds (200 kg spare); landing‑site selection requiring ≥ 2 wt% water within 200 km; emergency solid‑booster return capsule.  
*Severity:* Critical (2). *Likelihood:* Occasional (E). *Risk Index:* 2E (acceptable with contingency).

**Hazard H‑4: Loss of reactor cooling during interplanetary cruise.**  
*Causes:* Primary coolant loop leak; radiator puncture by micrometeorite; pump failure.  
*Controls:* Redundant coolant loops; self‑sealing radiator panels; backup thermoelectric generator for decay‑heat removal.  
*Severity:* Critical (2). *Likelihood:* Remote (D). *Risk Index:* 2D.

The integrated Probabilistic Risk Assessment (PRA) yields a Loss of Crew probability \(P_{\text{LOC}} \le 1/500\) per mission, consistent with the commercial crew threshold. The dominant risk contributors are EDL failure (\(P \approx 7 \times 10^{-4}\)), radiation medical event (\(5 \times 10^{-4}\)), ISRU return‑fuel failure (\(3 \times 10^{-4}\)), and micrometeorite penetration (\(2 \times 10^{-4}\)). The autonomy architecture contribution to \(P_{\text{LOC}}\) is below \(10^{-5}\).

